{"id": "EUVD-2026-81823", "enisaUuid": "c678f140-6969-34ef-b359-2496940c0292", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnvmet: fix heap out-of-bounds read in nvmet_auth_negotiate()\n\nnvmet_execute_auth_send() allocates the DH-HMAC-CHAP message buffer with\nthe host-supplied transfer length (tl) and hands it to\nnvmet_auth_negotiate() without passing tl along. nvmet_auth_negotiate()\nthen reads the negotiate header and, for each of the halen hash\nidentifiers and dhlen DH group identifiers, indexes into the fixed\nidlist[60] array (hashes at idlist[0..halen), groups at idlist[30..]).\n\nNeither the transfer length nor halen/dhlen is validated. A malicious or\nnon-conformant host can report a tl smaller than the negotiate structure,\nor a halen/dhlen larger than the array (both are u8, up to 255), making\nthe loops read past the end of the allocated buffer (heap out-of-bounds\nread). The sibling nvmet_auth_reply() already validates tl against the\nstructure size; the negotiate path did not.\n\nPass tl into nvmet_auth_negotiate(), reject a tl that does not cover the\nnegotiate data plus one full protocol descriptor, and reject halen/dhlen\nlarger than NVME_AUTH_DHCHAP_MAX_DH_IDS.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:07:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:00:06", "baseScore": 9.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/89ff11b72f38976f3b5aea23a5228ee05e277209", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aaac783950b17c57df9b6f7344747cacb1a407ed", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c38a8186326799957d293d370136c128cd113916", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7b81e4d2230e3d2d372c826180c4ef0efc244f31", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5bb96cc218835769ab74ec7f3ea2bf81fbffe955"], "aliases": ["GHSA-rrv7-jqj6-x46g", "CVE-2026-90230"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.46, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0d6eba08-5531-35b9-a0ae-3322b8bf8df3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "16476a96-fb10-3719-ba4b-a8ba64844185", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "1f7354cd-73bf-367f-938c-eca40350c491", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "db1312dd95488b5e6ff362ff66fcf953a46b1821 <aaac783950b17c57df9b6f7344747cacb1a407ed"}, {"id": "31f3e39a-b201-30db-8331-e2a12eb1e570", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "db1312dd95488b5e6ff362ff66fcf953a46b1821 <c38a8186326799957d293d370136c128cd113916"}, {"id": "58145a4b-45c8-3ed0-ae4c-dede6abf07d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "db1312dd95488b5e6ff362ff66fcf953a46b1821 <7b81e4d2230e3d2d372c826180c4ef0efc244f31"}, {"id": "59a21a2a-ae63-3324-b749-c175d8820927", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "db1312dd95488b5e6ff362ff66fcf953a46b1821 <89ff11b72f38976f3b5aea23a5228ee05e277209"}, {"id": "788dfb10-2401-3967-a41e-a7a2916b1d21", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.0"}, {"id": "90142447-e771-373c-90ec-63d7817a786f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "95b77010-2692-39b2-8dfe-f6855c21bfb6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "db1312dd95488b5e6ff362ff66fcf953a46b1821 <5bb96cc218835769ab74ec7f3ea2bf81fbffe955"}, {"id": "9b7aea3a-57f7-3d71-bf0b-3e7e5ea522d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "aa7f61c8-2e0c-33c4-93ea-50df79fe2911", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "dd1c9f36-6318-385d-8056-9f270bc90741", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor